From: yonglunyao <yonglunyao@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gaokun3: add scripts/ohos-check-dir.sh (from rk3568 kernel.patch)

Several OH common-module Kconfigs gate their symbols on
`def_bool $(success, $(srctree)/scripts/ohos-check-dir.sh ...)` —
SECURITY_XPM (security/xpm/Kconfig), UNIFIED_COLLECTION
(drivers/staging/ucollection), NEWIP (net/newip). The pristine
kernel_linux_6.6 tree does not carry the script; upstream boards get
it from their monolithic board patch (rk3568_patch/kernel.patch @
OpenHarmony-7.0-Release adds it as new file mode 100755, blob
2833618f9). Without it every $(success,...) check fails, the symbols
silently resolve to n during `make <board>_defconfig`, and the kernel
dies in asm-offsets with the latent one-arg PAGEFLAG_FALSE(XPMReadonly)
calls in include/linux/page-flags.h (the CONFIG_SECURITY_XPM #else
branch). Extracted verbatim from the proven rk3568 patch.
---
diff --git a/scripts/ohos-check-dir.sh b/scripts/ohos-check-dir.sh
new file mode 100755
index 000000000..2833618f9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/ohos-check-dir.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+#! /bin/bash
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+
+if [ -d "$1" ]; then
+    exit 0
+fi
+
+exit 1
